{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7e3c2a1-4f8d-4c6e-9a2b-1d5f7e9c0a3b",
    "name": "AlgoChat API — Server",
    "description": "📡 **AlgoChat — Complete REST API Collection (Server Side)**\n\nThis collection covers **every route** exposed by the AlgoChat Express server (`server/src/index.js`).\n\n## 🔐 Authentication\nAll routes except `Signup` and `Login` are protected by the `protectRoute` middleware (`server/src/middleware/auth.middleware.js`).\n- Auth type: **Bearer Token** (JWT, 7-day expiry)\n- The **Signup** and **Login** requests have a test script that automatically saves the returned JWT into the collection variable `{{token}}`, so you can run requests top-to-bottom without copy-pasting tokens.\n\n## 🚀 Quick Start\n1. Start the server: `cd server && npm run dev` (runs on `PORT=5001` by default).\n2. Run **Auth → Signup** (or **Login**) — the token is saved automatically.\n3. Set the `{{userId}}` collection variable to the `_id` of the user you want to chat with (copy it from **Messages → Get users for sidebar**).\n4. Run **Messages → Send message** and **Get messages**.\n\n## 🔌 Real-Time Events (Socket.io — reference, not testable via REST)\n| Event | Direction | Payload |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `getOnlineUsers` | Server → Client | `string[]` (userIds) |\n| `newMessage` | Server → Client | `Message` object |\n| `messageDelivered` | Client → Server | `{ messageId, senderId }` |\n| `messageRead` | Client → Server | `{ messageId, senderId }` |\n| `markAllMessagesAsRead` | Client → Server | `{ senderId, receiverId }` |\n| `messageStatusUpdate` | Server → Client | `{ messageId, status }` |\n| `allMessagesRead` | Server → Client | `{ receiverId }` |",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "algochat-server"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
